From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:11:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(plugins): add atomic empty-only path disposal [daveey]

Consumer: disk-cleanup `_sweep_empty_dirs` needs a nonrecursive kernel rmdir
through the shared executor. Checking emptiness then recursively deleting would
remove files arriving after observation. Keep the existing default, scope checks,
write denial, final-link handling and future custody veto in the same seam.

Add keyword-only empty_only=False to PluginContext.dispose_path and the executor.
True uses lstat then one os.rmdir, refuses non-directories and ENOTEMPTY/EEXIST,
and never falls back. Preserve host crossing and log the chosen mode.

This is the prerequisite seam-only PR for @task:hermes@hermes-hub/t_5885a5694e360983
(durable unpushed-source custody):
https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/3366
Original disposal seam:
https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/3951
The integration owner alone migrates disk-cleanup and adds custody policy.

Proof:
- scripts/run_tests.sh: disposal/context/host/disk-cleanup/boundary suites:
  103 passed, 1 macOS-only skip; final expanded disposal suite: 40 passed.
- scripts/hermes-python scripts/check --base origin/main: passed.
- Original 19 disposal cases and helpers unchanged (AST comparison); plugin API
  manifest, boundary baseline and disk-cleanup sources unchanged.
- RED/GREEN: removing the empty_only branch (fallthrough to existing rmtree /
  unlink) produced 3 failures: nonempty, arrival[True], symlink. The False arrival
  control passed. Restoring the branch passed all 4 selected cases. Canonical
  runner with file retries disabled; no fabricated outputs.
- Additional coverage: EEXIST/ENOTEMPTY, PermissionError/EBUSY/ENOTDIR, strict bool,
  write-denied and root refusals, host equality, logging, and arrival immediately
  before the sole real kernel rmdir with target-scan/recursive/unlink tripwires.

